def find_rotation_count(arr):
    low = 0
    high = len(arr) - 1

    while low <= high:
        if arr[low] <= arr[high]:
            return low

        mid = (low + high) // 2
        next_index = (mid + 1) % len(arr)
        prev_index = (mid - 1 + len(arr)) % len(arr)

        if arr[mid] <= arr[next_index] and arr[mid] <= arr[prev_index]:
            return mid
        elif arr[mid] <= arr[high]:
            high = mid - 1
        else:
            low = mid + 1
```

This function uses binary search to efficiently find the index of the smallest element in the rotated sorted array, which indicates the number of rotations required to get the original sorted order.

